---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const pageTitle = 'Terms of Service — FormFix';
const pageDescription = 'FormFix Terms of Service. User responsibilities, independent service disclaimers, and exam requirement verification guidance.';
---

<BaseLayout title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container content-container">
      <div class="tool-header">
        <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="lead-text">Last updated: February 2026. Please read these terms carefully before using FormFix.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>1. Acceptable Use</h2>
        <p>FormFix provides web-based image manipulation utilities for personal, educational, and non-commercial application preparation. By accessing or using FormFix, you agree to use the service in compliance with applicable laws and not to attempt to disrupt or tamper with website assets or infrastructure.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>2. Independent Service & Exam Authority Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>FormFix is an <strong>independent utility website</strong>. FormFix is <strong>not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or officially connected to any government agency, examination body, or recruitment board</strong>, including but not limited to SSC, UPSC, IBPS, NTA, RRB, or state public service commissions.</p>
        <p>All trademarks, exam names, and official notification titles cited on FormFix belong exclusively to their respective owners. Their mention does not imply any official relationship or endorsement.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>3. Requirement Accuracy & User Verification Responsibility</h2>
        <p>FormFix compiles photo, signature, and document specifications from publicly available official notifications. However, examination authorities frequently update file size limits, pixel dimensions, background color requirements, and format rules between notification cycles.</p>
        <p><strong>Important:</strong> Users are solely responsible for verifying their specific application requirements against the current, official recruitment notification issued by the respective authority prior to submitting their application.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>4. No Guarantee of Application Acceptance</h2>
        <p>While FormFix provides validation checks based on recorded criteria, FormFix does not guarantee that files processed on this site will be accepted by third-party application portals. Acceptance remains under the sole discretion of the receiving exam authority or portal software.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>5. Service Availability & Modifications</h2>
        <p>FormFix is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis without warranties of any kind. We reserve the right to modify, update, or discontinue tools, presets, or features at any time without prior notice.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>6. Intellectual Property</h2>
        <p>The code, brand design, interface components, and custom content of FormFix are protected by applicable copyright laws. You may not reproduce, duplicate, or redistribute website code or layout assets without permission.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, FormFix and its creators shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages resulting from the use of, or inability to use, our tools or information presented on the website.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card content-card">
        <h2>8. Contact Information</h2>
        <p>Questions regarding these Terms of Service may be directed to our team via the <a href="/contact">Contact Page</a> or by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@formfix.me">contact@formfix.me</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .content-container {
    max-width: 768px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .lead-text {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  .content-card {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3.5vw, 2rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }

  .content-card h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-bold);
    color: var(--color-gray-900);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
  }

  .content-card p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    max-width: none;
  }
</style>
